  "body": "## Production-readiness Stage 1: coverage / gaps\n\nThis PR forks released SCAN v0.28.0 into the v0.29 candidate and implements only the first production-readiness tranche.\n\n### Added\n\n- automatic `coverage_report.json`\n- compact `coverage_report.md`\n- unresolved `gaps.md`\n- explicit `scan-body coverage-report` regeneration command\n- projection-manifest sealing for all three outputs\n- refresh support after legitimate canonical overlay/reconstruction promotion\n- v0.29 release qualification now requires these outputs\n- tracked production-readiness gate document\n\n### Authority boundary\n\n`scan_index.sqlite` remains canonical.\n\nThe new projection:\n- opens canonical data read-only;\n- cannot promote or downgrade MAPPED/PARTIAL/BLOCKED/UNKNOWN;\n- reuses existing surface/effect closure rather than reimplementing it;\n- retains canonical IDs/evidence IDs;\n- deliberately emits **no scalar confidence score**.\n\n### Executed evidence so far\n\nDedicated v0.29 candidate workflow:\n- **163 passed, 1 skipped**\n- duplicate coverage-report bytes: PASS\n- projection manifest verification: PASS\n- canonical SQLite row determinism: PASS\n- v0.28 \u2192 v0.29 canonical row parity on the qualification fixture: PASS\n- exact report-count reconciliation to SQLite: PASS\n\nFrozen NotepadNext/Moji v0.28\u2192v0.29 calibration is running as the remaining Stage-1 real-specimen gate.\n\n### Explicitly out of scope\n\nNo uncertainty challenger, triage ranking, layered-provenance redesign, parity-scenario system, runtime validation, or other later roadmap stage is included in this PR.\n\nThe inherited v0.28 `PACKAGE_MANIFEST.json` was removed; v0.29 is not release-sealed.",
